WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.440
Believe it or not, The Lost Boys was originally
supposed to be a more wholesome, Peter Pan-inspired

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.680
vampire movie. But following the success of
St. Elmo's Fire, director Joel Schumacher

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.220
turned the project into a sexy, gory, and
politically subversive teenage classic that

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.689
changed the way vampires would be portrayed
in Hollywood for decades to come.

00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:22.650
While it still holds up as one of the better
vampire films ever made, there's probably

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.449
a lot you don't know about this cult classic.
So grab your leather jacket, hold onto the

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:31.380
rails, and check out the untold truth of The
Lost Boys.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.809
Santa Carla

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:36.699
You don't have to be from California to know
that Santa Carla, the town where The Lost

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:41.420
Boys takes place, doesn't actually exist.
However, locals can easily recognize The Lost

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:46.510
Boys' location as the South Bay beach town
Santa Cruz, thanks to shots of its Giant Dipper

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.000
Roller Coaster.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.359
Director Joel Schumacher fell in love with
the locale as soon as he scouted it, telling

00:00:51.359 --> 00:00:55.930
the local news, "The movie didn't come together
until I saw [Santa Cruz]. At the time, there

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:00.579
was an enormous amount of transient kids moving
through Santa Cruz. This is exactly where

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:03.250
I would come if I was a teenage vampire."

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:07.330
After reversing a couple of letters in nearby
Santa Clara, he even had a locally inspired

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.390
new name for his movie's dream spot.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.150
The cast enjoyed filming in the scenic beach
town, too. Corey Feldman recalled, "We had

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:17.250
such a great time there. Being kids and having
the opportunity to be at the Boardwalk every

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:22.390
day, getting to ride on the Giant Dipper and
being at the beach, it was such a fun experience."

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:27.030
However, securing Santa Cruz as the film's
location wasn't all smooth sailing. The town's

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:31.020
authorities were wary of the Boardwalk being
portrayed in a bad light, especially after

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.250
1983's violent Sudden Impact took them by
surprise. Even worse, Santa Carla's title

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:40.470
as "the murder capital of the world" wasn't
fictional, as Santa Cruz earned that description

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:44.910
after years of serial killings. But the authorities
read The Lost Boys' script, loved it, and

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:49.610
ended up giving Schumacher the green light.
And the rest is pop culture history.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.270
Goonies gone vampire

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:56.080
The Lost Boys was initially skewed towards
a much younger audience. The film's original

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:01.310
script, written by Jan Fischer and James Jeremias,
was intended to be — as the title suggests

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:06.180
— a re-imagining of Peter Pan with vampires.
However, as Schumacher told the Telegraph,

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:10.140
he thought it read too much like "The Goonies
go vampire," especially with Goonies director

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:14.160
Richard Donner originally at the helm and
Corey Feldman joining the cast.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.250
When Donner departed the project to direct
Lethal Weapon, Schumacher gained control and

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.090
took The Lost Boys from "very wholesome" to
very campy.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.740
He explained, "The Frog brothers were Boy
Scouts. I thought, 'Why can't they all be

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.110
teenagers? Why can't they be dressed incredibly?
And why can't they have stripped-down motorcycles

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.220
that look skeletal?'"

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:34.950
Schumacher posed these questions to Warner
Bros. president Mark Canton, who ultimately

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.770
gave him permission to give the script a teenage
makeover.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:42.140
Alex Winter, who played Marko, praised the
changes, saying, "I don't think I really connected

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.410
with it until I got there and realized quite
how deep Joel was going. He really got it

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:50.410
cinematically and was taking it to this crazy
place."

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.100
Edgar Rambo

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:55.490
Thanks to his connection with Goonies director
Richard Donner, Corey Feldman received an

00:02:55.490 --> 00:03:00.590
invitation to audition for the part of The
Lost Boys' vampire-slaying Edgar Frog. But

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.970
when he read through the script with Joel
Schumacher, he got an interesting note:

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:10.780
"He was like, 'That was great but could you
maybe, um, butch it up a little bit?'"

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:14.209
Feldman said he was instructed to hit the
video store and rent the movies of Sylvester

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:16.190
Stallone and Chuck Norris, telling him:

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:21.440
"That is your character. I want you to meld
all of these guys together and make something

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:22.440
out of it."

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:26.130
Feldman's portrayal of Edgar Frog certainly
breathes some comedic life into the film,

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:29.020
which is often pretty dark and serious.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.710
Of that Feldman said, "I think the fun part
about the character and the comic value of

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:36.290
it is that he doesn't think it's funny, and
he's not in on the joke. So, [he's] one of

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:40.599
those people that you just kinda have to laugh
at because, you know, they really take themselves

00:03:40.599 --> 00:03:44.930
very seriously, and they believe every word
of what they're saying about themselves, or

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.210
whatever it is they believe in."

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.660
Challenging conventions

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:53.860
The Lost Boys may be campy, but it also challenged
certain common conventions about family life

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:54.940
in America.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:59.550
The Atlantic argues that the movie arrived
at a time when many Americans were fearful

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:03.510
of a perceived disintegration of the traditional
nuclear family structure.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:07.550
The Lost Boys challenged these notions by
focusing on two non-traditional families — the

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:12.489
Emersons and the vampire crew. As 'the good
guys,' the Emersons survive — and ultimately

00:04:12.489 --> 00:04:16.430
thrive — despite the mother being newly
divorced, broke, and forced to move into her

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:20.650
father's house with her two sons. When we
meet Max — the one father-type character

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:24.930
who could offer a traditional fix to the broken
Emerson family — it turns out he's also

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:30.229
a monster. Meanwhile, the film's other family
is a bunch of dudes living, sleeping, partying,

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:31.430
and killing together.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:37.240
Additionally, the film is also commonly analyzed
as challenging conservative notions of sexuality,

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:40.710
all at a time when the President of the United
States was accused of ignoring the country's

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.849
incredibly serious AIDS crisis.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:47.820
Today, much of The Lost Boys is commonly viewed
as homoerotic. Santa Carla itself represents

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:52.449
a place where people on the outskirts of society,
such as homosexuals and vampires, can live

00:04:52.449 --> 00:04:57.120
openly. David and his crew of vampires dress
in leather outfits not unlike to those worn

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.389
by members of the early '80's underground
gay club scene, and new vampires must drink

00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:06.059
David's blood in an initiation ceremony. Sam's
bedroom is decorated with a poster of Rob

00:05:06.059 --> 00:05:11.189
Lowe's abs. Michael, fearing his actions with
David have led him down a deviant path, rushes

00:05:11.189 --> 00:05:15.650
off to have sex with Star — whom none of
the other vampires seem particularly interested

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:16.650
in.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:21.620
Schumacher himself even endorses these analyses,
telling GamesRadar that "[The Lost Boys] is,

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:27.099
in a way, about the fear we have of the Other—those
who live outside of the mainstream."

00:05:27.099 --> 00:05:28.680
All about Michael

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:33.479
Anyone who's ever even passively watched The
Lost Boys has the name "Michael" permanently

00:05:33.479 --> 00:05:37.809
engraved in their memories of the movie. That's
because the protagonist's name is uttered

00:05:37.809 --> 00:05:40.879
more than any other word in the entire film.

00:05:40.879 --> 00:05:44.099
Just how many times do we hear his name? Well
over a hundred.

00:05:44.099 --> 00:05:48.289
"Michael! Michael! Michael! Michael! Michael!
Michael! Michael!"

00:05:48.289 --> 00:05:52.319
Considering the film's runtime is only 97
minutes, that means viewers got at least one

00:05:52.319 --> 00:05:57.370
Michael-mention a minute, which is a lotta
name love for one half-vampire to receive.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.869
A Tale of Two Coreys

00:05:59.869 --> 00:06:04.589
Child stars Corey Haim and Corey Feldman were
a late '80s dynamic duo, appearing together

00:06:04.589 --> 00:06:09.400
in pics like License to Drive, Dream a Little
Dream, and National Lampoon's Last Resort.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:13.199
But it was The Lost Boys that first paired
the young actors who'd later be referred to

00:06:13.199 --> 00:06:14.740
as "the two Coreys."

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:20.300
"We just clicked. Uh, chemistry for ourselves,
and people I guess get wind of it. Like 'Wow,

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:23.530
these two have something off camera but on
camera.'"

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:27.979
Unfortunately, a series of ill-advised personal
and professional decisions derailed both Coreys'

00:06:27.979 --> 00:06:33.310
careers, and their brief peak as teenage heartthrobs
belied a slew of direct-to-video releases.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:37.539
Sadly, even their on-screen reunion on the
short-lived reality show The Two Coreys couldn't

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:43.349
save Corey Haim, who passed away in 2010 at
the age of 38.

00:06:43.349 --> 00:06:45.380
Ben Stiller, Lost Boy?

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:49.599
Kiefer Sutherland's crew of leather-wearing
teenage vampires with rock 'n' roll haircuts

00:06:49.599 --> 00:06:53.039
almost included another up-and-comer we all
know now.

00:06:53.039 --> 00:06:57.289
Ben Stiller has claimed that he was almost
cast as one of the Lost Boys, telling a Hollywood

00:06:57.289 --> 00:07:02.509
crowd in 2010, "Last time I saw a room full
of so many talented faces was when I auditioned

00:07:02.509 --> 00:07:06.999
for The Lost Boys. It was between me and Kiefer
and the two Coreys."

00:07:06.999 --> 00:07:10.869
He might've been joking, but the actor would
have been 21 at the time of production, which

00:07:10.869 --> 00:07:13.460
makes him the right age for one of the roles.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:17.869
It's also fairly easy to imagine the dark-haired
Stiller wearing leather and riding a motorcycle

00:07:17.869 --> 00:07:22.879
alongside Sutherland and crew. Considering
all the models that did make into the cast,

00:07:22.879 --> 00:07:27.449
it's also easy to picture Zoolander's patented
"Blue Steel" pose stacking up against Brooke

00:07:27.449 --> 00:07:30.860
McCarter's tough-guy smirk quite nicely.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.879
Stolen fiancée

00:07:32.879 --> 00:07:37.430
While filming The Lost Boys, Jason Patric
and Kiefer Sutherland became close friends.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:41.919
Four years later, however, Patric was on an
airplane to Ireland with Sutherland's ex-fiancée,

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:45.279
Julia Roberts, leading to some juicy tabloid
drama.

00:07:45.279 --> 00:07:49.150
In 2016, Sutherland reflected on the headline-making
breakup from years earlier:

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:54.930
"We were young and we were both very much
in love, and we had decided that we wanted

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:59.919
to get married… She was arguably the most
famous woman in the world… This wedding

00:07:59.919 --> 00:08:04.719
that was supposed to be something between
the two of us became something so big… I

00:08:04.719 --> 00:08:09.059
think she had the courage — it wasn't what
she wanted to do in the end."

00:08:09.059 --> 00:08:12.879
Not long after her split with Sutherland,
however, Roberts started dating Patric. For

00:08:12.879 --> 00:08:16.960
his part, Patric has since downplayed the
whole love triangle ordeal, telling Vulture,

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:21.270
"everything that happened was all fake and
bulls--- and let them give quotes about whatever

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:25.729
they want. Obviously people are gonna ask.
They had a relationship that ended and I was

00:08:25.729 --> 00:08:29.659
with her for a little while and it ended.
They've both been subsequently married several

00:08:29.659 --> 00:08:34.099
times and I think they're fine. But we never
had any issue, even back then."

00:08:34.099 --> 00:08:38.019
Indeed, to this day, Patric claims he has
maintained his friendship with Sutherland,

00:08:38.019 --> 00:08:39.979
despite their brief romantic rivalry.

00:08:39.979 --> 00:08:43.599
"It's just nice that all these years later,
I'm still very good friend with Jami Gertz,

00:08:43.599 --> 00:08:47.259
very good friends with Kiefer. And, it was
a special time."

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:49.430
Buffy the vampire stealer

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:53.690
As one of the first teenage vampire films
to feature some serious sex appeal, The Lost

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:59.060
Boys inspired a whole new sub-genre of vampire
stories — including Buffy the Vampire Slayer.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:03.190
Buffy creator Joss Whedon has gone on record
to explain some of the ways his movie and

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:08.339
resulting TV series took inspiration from
the film. As Whedon told Salon back in 2003,

00:09:08.339 --> 00:09:12.470
"the idea of [vampires] looking like monsters
and then looking like people … That was

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:17.899
in Lost Boys, and that was very useful for
us. … You could have somebody fool you,

00:09:17.899 --> 00:09:21.770
or someone like Angel seem like he's not a
vampire and then he is one."

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:26.130
The series' second season introduced a character
named Spike, a platinum blonde vampire played

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:30.610
by James Marsters. Whedon credited The Lost
Boys for the inspiration for the character,

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:34.620
saying "there's a little Billy Idol, a little
Kiefer Sutherland in The Lost Boys, and every

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:36.810
guy in a black coat."

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:38.389
Skip the sequels

00:09:38.389 --> 00:09:42.839
Although The Lost Boys lives on as a piece
of cultural iconography, its sequels definitely

00:09:42.839 --> 00:09:44.930
failed to earn the same kind of hype.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:50.120
Why? Well, the first sequel took 20 years
to happen, and even then it was still a straight-to-DVD

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:55.240
sort of deal. Titled Lost Boys: The Tribe,
the movie did bring back Corey Feldman as

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.889
the only original cast member who made it
into the final cut. And while it features

00:09:58.889 --> 00:10:03.610
plenty of vampires and topless women, it has
almost nothing to do with the original film,

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:07.540
leading critics to unanimously label it as
little more than a cheap cash grab.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:11.790
It did manage to make back its production
costs upon release, however, so Warner Bros.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:15.990
gave the go ahead to another titled Lost Boys:
The Thirst, featuring the reunion of Feldman

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:20.440
and Jamison Newlander as the Frog brothers.
However, it was slaughtered by critics and

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:25.490
sold half as many DVDs as the first sequel
… so consider this one a lost boy in its

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:26.699
own right.

00:10:26.699 --> 00:10:29.690
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.360
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

